{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"98df55d5d1e69fd2","name":"card_event_orp_general_haller","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Poland/events/card_event_orp_general_haller","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"ORP GENERAL HALLER","text":"Convert target unit and adjacent units into ROUTED TROOPS.","flavorText":"ORP General Haller was a Polish Navy gunboat originally constructed in 1916 at the Crichton-Vulcan shipyard in Turku, Finland, for the Imperial Russian Navy. After Poland regained independence in 1918, the vessel was acquired in 1921 and renamed in honor of General Józef Haller, a leading figure in the Polish military. The ship measured 55 meters long, displaced 342 tons, and was armed with two 76mm guns, four machine guns, and could carry up to 30 naval mines. During the interwar years, Generał Haller served mainly as a training ship and minelayer. By 1939, she formed part of Poland’s small coastal defense force. At the outbreak of WWII, she was stationed at Gdynia under the command of Captain Stanisław Mieszkowski. Following German air attacks, the gunboat moved to the Hel Peninsula where her weapons were stripped and used to strengthen land-based coastal defenses. On 6 September 1939, ORP General Haller was sunk by Luftwaffe bombing.","faction":"Poland","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":8,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"GameplayTags":["subtype.navy"],"Name":"card_event_orp_general_haller","title":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_orp_general_haller_title","SourceString":"ORP GENERAL HALLER","LocalizedString":"ORP GENERAL HALLER"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Poland","kredits":8,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_orp_general_haller_text","SourceString":"Convert target unit and adjacent units into ROUTED TROOPS.","LocalizedString":"Convert target unit and adjacent units into ROUTED TROOPS."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_orp_general_haller_history","SourceString":"ORP General Haller was a Polish Navy gunboat originally constructed in 1916 at the Crichton-Vulcan shipyard in Turku, Finland, for the Imperial Russian Navy. After Poland regained independence in 1918, the vessel was acquired in 1921 and renamed in honor of General Józef Haller, a leading figure in the Polish military. The ship measured 55 meters long, displaced 342 tons, and was armed with two 76mm guns, four machine guns, and could carry up to 30 naval mines. During the interwar years, Generał Haller served mainly as a training ship and minelayer. By 1939, she formed part of Poland’s small coastal defense force. At the outbreak of WWII, she was stationed at Gdynia under the command of Captain Stanisław Mieszkowski. Following German air attacks, the gunboat moved to the Hel Peninsula where her weapons were stripped and used to strengthen land-based coastal defenses. On 6 September 1939, ORP General Haller was sunk by Luftwaffe bombing.","LocalizedString":"ORP General Haller was a Polish Navy gunboat originally constructed in 1916 at the Crichton-Vulcan shipyard in Turku, Finland, for the Imperial Russian Navy. After Poland regained independence in 1918, the vessel was acquired in 1921 and renamed in honor of General Józef Haller, a leading figure in the Polish military. The ship measured 55 meters long, displaced 342 tons, and was armed with two 76mm guns, four machine guns, and could carry up to 30 naval mines. During the interwar years, Generał Haller served mainly as a training ship and minelayer. By 1939, she formed part of Poland’s small coastal defense force. At the outbreak of WWII, she was stationed at Gdynia under the command of Captain Stanisław Mieszkowski. Following German air attacks, the gunboat moved to the Hel Peninsula where her weapons were stripped and used to strengthen land-based coastal defenses. On 6 September 1939, ORP General Haller was sunk by Luftwaffe bombing."},"rarity":"ERarityE